# README gap 3, second half -- FIXED 2026-08-27 by `mul`, though the
# `*` TOKEN is still refused and stays that way by design.
#
# Maths beyond `+` arrives as FUNCTIONS: `-` `*` `/` `%` stay reserved
# (test/spec/op-chars.tsv), so `2 * 1999` is still a parse refusal and
# `mul(2, 1999)` is how it is said. The seed's "qty 2 spelled unit +
# unit" workaround is no longer needed, and neither is computing VAT
# off-model.
#
# The family refuses what `+` would silently answer: `add("500m",
# "500m")` is an error where `"500m" + "500m"` is the string
# "500m500m", which is how a Kubernetes quantity becomes nonsense.
# run: aontu gaps/multiply.aon
# expected: {"amount":3998,"tenPercent":399,"vatCents":759}
# actual:   {"amount":3998,"tenPercent":399,"vatCents":759}
amount: mul(2, 1999)
# 19% VAT on 3998 cents, in integer cents: multiply FIRST, then divide,
# so the one truncation happens at the end. 19% of 3998 is 759.62, and
# div truncates toward zero, so the answer is 759 -- which is the
# rounding rule stated once rather than inherited from a host.
vatCents: div(mul($.amount, 19), 100)
tenPercent: div($.amount, 10)
